2:T458,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"The 4 Leadership Archetypes at Work: Shifting From Prover to Sovereign","description":"Explore the 4 Workplace Leadership Archetypes (Victim, Prover, Performer, Sovereign) and learn how upgrading your executive identity and team assumptions accelerates performance.","datePublished":"2026-11-18","dateModified":"2026-11-24","articleSection":"Business & Workplace","keywords":"leadership archetypes at work, sovereign leadership, executive presence and identity, overcoming executive burnout, collective assumptions organizational culture, vibrational leadership in business, how to stop micromanaging","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://vibehyr.com/blog/vibrational-leadership-four-archetypes-collective-assumptions"},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Keisha Solomon","jobTitle":"Founder & Master Architect, Vibe Hyr"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe Hyr","url":"https://vibehyr.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://vibehyr.com/icons/icon-512.png"}},"image":"https://vibehyr.com/images/og-image.png"}3:T57c,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the Four Archetypes at Work in Vibrational Leadership?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Four Archetypes are The Victim (reactive, blames external blockers), The Prover (ties self-worth to overwork, urgency, and rescuing others), The Performer (optimizes for optics and politics rather than truth), and The Sovereign (leads from internal certainty, clear standards, and calm decision-making)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does \"The Prover\" archetype hurt team productivity?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"When a leader operates as The Prover — answering messages late at night and taking back difficult tasks to make sure they are done right — they broadcast an unspoken assumption of anxiety and distrust. Capable team members unconsciously adapt by becoming passive waiters rather than autonomous problem-solvers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a Team Collective Assumption Audit?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A Team Collective Assumption Audit is a structured retrospective where a team identifies its repeated complaints or limiting stories (e.g., \"Enterprise deals always stall in legal\"), recognizes how that shared expectation filters their behavior, and installs a new operational standard backed by concrete process changes."}}]}8:["slug","vibrational-leadership-four-archetypes-collective-assumptions","d"]
